Complete local Rust example; the app itself does not execute it:
```rust

enum List { Cons(i32, Box<List>), Nil }
impl List {
    fn sum(&self) -> i32 {
        match self { Self::Cons(n, tail) => n + tail.sum(), Self::Nil => 0 }
    }
}
fn main() {
    let list = List::Cons(3, Box::new(List::Cons(4, Box::new(List::Nil))));
    println!("{}", list.sum());
}
```

